    {
      "id": "atomic-durable-fan-out-receipt",
      "type": "positive",
      "statement": "One transaction creates one source-event receipt and one immutable delivery per bound instance. Composite foreign keys bind each WorkItem to its instance and each Run to its WorkItem; transactional validation requires the initial transition. Real fan-out and concurrent submissions converge, and lock waiters re-read the receipt before orphan checks. Partial fan-out, cross-link reuse, more than 43 targets, absent commit, and post-audit faults leave no partial receipt.",
      "test_refs": [
